# =====================================================================
#  GR33N - what does NOT go into the repository
# =====================================================================

# --- build output ----------------------------------------------------
build/
*.elf
*.self
*.pkg
*.map
*.o

# xmb/ is produced by 'sh deps/install-xmb.sh' from pkgfiles/ and sfo.xml.
# What's inside is a copy; the originals are in the repository and it comes
# out the same on any machine.
#
# (pkgfiles/ DOES go in the repository: the PNGs are hand-made and nothing
# generates them. Two directories looking alike doesn't make them the same.)
xmb/

# --- the PC tests ----------------------------------------------------
#
# They're not needed to build GR33N and never were: they test the
# arithmetic on a PC, under ASan and UBSan, and they were the working tools
# while this was being written.
t/

# --- THE PRIVATE FOLDER. THIS LINE DOESN'T GET TOUCHED. --------------
#
# privado/ is everything used to get here that isn't needed to build or run
# GR33N: the platform probes, working notes, backups of files taken before
# changing them, the test server from the v0.3.0 loop.
#
# And, above all, privado/token.dat and privado/config.cfg.
privado/

# --- THE ACTUAL SECRETS ----------------------------------------------
#
# token.dat is the Microsoft account transfer token, IN THE CLEAR. It
# starts with "M.C517_BAY.0.U.MsaArtifacts." and with that alone anyone
# gets into the Xbox account of whoever built this. It lives in privado/,
# but it's named here too in case it ever comes back to the root: one extra
# line costs nothing, and the missing one costs an account.
token.dat
*.token

# config.cfg holds the chosen region, the language and the dead zone of
# SOMEONE'S pad. It does no harm, but it has no business in the repository
# either: the next person to clone would get someone else's preferences.
config.cfg

# --- THE LOGS. THIS ONE DOESN'T GET TOUCHED EITHER. ------------------
#
# Anything from before 0.28.2 carries the Microsoft token and the SRTP
# session keys IN THE CLEAR: they were logged whole before linkRedact()
# existed. One is enough.
#
# Verified: gr33n-20260824-124012.log contained an SRTP key in the clear.
# This isn't theoretical.
#
# Before any push, LOOK at 'git status' and confirm not one .log shows up.
# Trusting this line is not enough: a file git already tracks is not
# unprotected by a .gitignore added afterwards.
logs/
*.log

# --- backups taken before changing something -------------------------
*.antes-de-*
*.bak
*.orig

# --- leftovers from mistyped commands --------------------------------
#
# These came from redirections with a Spanish sentence behind them:
# "> mirando la 17 cabeceras compilando el ...". Zero bytes each. They're
# named here so that if they ever reappear they don't slip through.
17
cabeceras
compilando
el
la
mirando
tipos

# --- what the editor leaves behind -----------------------------------
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
